course: dictionary
lesson: 6482
title: Naval
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Naval is a word that tells you what something belongs to. Look at «James Cook, a British naval captain, made three great voyages.» The word naval sits in front of captain, and a captain is a person in charge of a ship. So naval tells you the captain served in a navy, the armed forces that fight and travel at sea.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Sentences about warships, sailors, battles and bases often use naval. Try swapping in a word you know, such as sea, and see if the meaning still fits. It is close, but a sea captain could sail a ferry. A naval captain is in the navy, so naval is the more exact word.
explain: Naval is an adjective, which means it describes a noun. We say a naval battle, a naval base, a naval officer and naval history. Each phrase is about a navy, its ships or its people.
fact: Naval means to do with a navy, warships or sailors in the armed forces.
fact: Naval is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «naval battle».
fact: The Battle of Trafalgar in 1805 was a naval battle, which Admiral Nelson's British fleet won.
fact: The Battle of Midway in 1942 was a naval battle in the Pacific.
fact: Naval bases, ships and history often appear in lessons about empires and wars.
exercise: «James Cook, a British naval captain, made three great voyages.» What does naval mean here? | To do with music | Very quiet | To do with farming | *To do with a navy or warships
exercise: Which of these is a naval officer? | A teacher of music | *An officer in a country's navy | A chef who cooks on a train | A farmer who grows wheat
exercise: In which lesson would you most likely read about a naval battle? | *A history lesson about the Battle of Trafalgar | An art lesson about paint | A cooking lesson about bread | A maths lesson about shapes
test: «Midway in 1942 was a famous naval battle.» What does naval tell you about the battle? | It was a party with music | It was fought on land by soldiers only | It was a race between runners | *It was fought by navy ships and sailors
test: Which of these is an example of naval history? | *The navy's battles and voyages over hundreds of years | The rules of chess | The names of birds in a garden | The menu of a seaside café
exam: Cook was a naval captain who mapped islands; what does naval tell you about his job? | He was a gardener | He was a painter | He ran a shop | *He served in a navy
